/// Subject: Holo Hosting proof-of-service — one agreement settles host payment for
/// BOTH Holo services, EdgeNode and WindTunnel. The execution logic is identical;
/// only the invoice payload differs (an EdgeNode invoice fills gossip/storage,
/// a WindTunnel invoice fills its two placeholders).
///
/// Users:
/// - EdgeNode Customer (spender + list publisher): funds the agreement with
///   base-unit credit, fixes the price sheet at creation, maintains the host
///   allow-list, and receives the per-dimension metering record.
/// - Log Harvester (invoicing gateway, canonical executor): parks the host
///   work-proofs and runs settlements.
/// - EdgeNode Hosts (receivers): paid per the metered work in their logs — but
///   ONLY while on the customer's allow-list (default-deny).
///
/// Inputs:
/// - edge_node_customer_spender_allocations: base-unit credit the customer parked
///   to fund host payment (auto-generated by the pre-processor).
/// - invoice_payloads: per-host work-proofs; each carries host_pub_key and logs
///   (the metered counts s/g/wt1/wt2).
/// - initial_allow_list (Fixed): the hosts allowed at creation. `[]` when the
///   hosters aren't known yet — the customer then seeds the list with delta
///   parks before the first settlement. Any settlement that would consume an
///   invoice for a host the list does not name throws instead (see the
///   unpayable guard below), so settling before the seed lands — or after a
///   mid-period removal, or with a mistyped key — is a retryable error, never
///   silent loss of the hosts' work.
/// - discard_unpayable (ExecutorProvided, optional): true → settle anyway when
///   invoices name hosts that are off the allow-list, consuming that work
///   unpaid. The deliberate counterpart to the unpayable guard: use it when the
///   customer really does mean to drop the excluded host's parked work rather
///   than allow it. Discarded invoices cannot be re-submitted.
/// - allow_list_deltas: consumable data parks by the `list_publisher` role (the
///   customer). Each park's payload carries
///   `allow_list_deltas: { add: [pubkeys], remove: [pubkeys] }`. Deltas apply to
///   the standing list at the next settlement and the park is consumed (deleted)
///   by it — the updated list then rides forward in the RAVE's
///   `carryover.allow_list`, so the standing list is always
///   previous-carryover (or initial_allow_list on the first run) + this run's
///   deltas. All adds apply before all removes — deterministic regardless of
///   park discovery order; an agent added and removed in the same period ends up
///   removed. Deltas are AUTHOR-GATED in this script via
///   `get_spend_links_author`: a park not authored by funds_owner_pubkey is
///   ignored (it is still consumed). ROLE QUALIFICATION IS THE PRIMARY CONTROL,
///   not this gate: the DNA enforces it on parked links, so qualifying
///   `list_publisher` to the customer means a stranger cannot create the park
///   at all. The sample does that, and every instance should. What the gate
///   adds is the tie to `funds_owner_pubkey` specifically — that key and the
///   role's qualification are separate settings that nothing cross-checks, so
///   on an instance where they disagree (or one left qualified as `Any`) this
///   is what keeps the list in the funds owner's hands. The author it compares
///   is validator-derived, never payload-supplied.
///   TRUST NOTE — what the chain enforces, precisely, and where it stops.
///   THIS RUN'S DELTAS ARE ENFORCED: role qualification on parked links keeps
///   an unqualified agent from creating one, and consumed-input binding ties
///   each delta's value to the parked link it names, so the executor can
///   neither forge a delta nor rewrite one. THE CARRIED LIST IS NOT: it arrives
///   through `previous_execution`, a `Custom` input, and validation re-derives
///   `locked` from the real predecessor (Rule 7) while doing nothing equivalent
///   for `carryover`. A dishonest executor can therefore present a
///   `carryover.allow_list` naming hosts the customer never added, and the DNA
///   accepts it — the customer's locked funding then pays hosts they excluded.
///   Under the canonical harvester-executor instance that is a trust statement
///   about Holo for the CARRIED portion only; every customer park is their own
///   signed statement on the DHT, so divergence is provable after the fact.
///   Closing it needs DNA-side re-derivation of `carryover` from the actual
///   predecessor, the way Rule 7 already re-derives `locked`. Two mitigations
///   today: a customer who re-states their full list as a fresh delta each
///   period keeps the enforced portion current and the forgeable window short;
///   a customer who needs it enforced outright must execute the agreement
///   themselves (sole AuthorizedExecutor = the customer), which keeps
///   carry-forward but gives up Holo-runs-settlement.
/// - price_sheet_data_blob_hash (Fixed): the price sheet — per-dimension base
///   rates (base_per_st/gsp/wt1/wt2).
/// - funds_owner_pubkey (Fixed): the customer/publisher key — the agent paid by
///   `unlock` and the metering credit, and the only author whose allow-list
///   deltas count.
/// - unlock (ExecutorProvided, optional): true → return the whole held balance to
///   funds_owner_pubkey and settle nothing. Only the executor can trigger it, so
///   under the canonical harvester-executor instance the customer's reclaim
///   requires the harvester's cooperation. Caution: run it only when no invoices
///   are parked — parked invoices consumed by an unlock run are discarded unpaid.
///
/// Instances must name a sole AuthorizedExecutor — the agreement locks its
/// unspent funding (carry-forward), which the DNA rejects under
/// ExecutorRules::Any. Canonically that executor is the Log Harvester, so
/// settlement runs reliably on Holo's cadence while the customer keeps
/// exclusive control of funding and the allow-list through their parks.
///
/// Summary:
/// Prices each ALLOWED host's logged work against the Fixed price sheet and
/// settles it from the customer's base-unit credit; unspent funding locks and
/// carries forward. The metered dimensions are pinned to FIXED unit indices,
/// matching the order a Holo Hosting network registers its units in (indices
/// are positions in the global unit registry, assigned as units are created):
///   "0" HF, the base fuel unit host payment is drawn from · "1" HOT, which
///   this agreement does not touch · "2" BW (bandwidth), metered as gossip
///   · "3" ST (storage) · "4" WTUP and "5" WTRUN, the WindTunnel placeholders
/// A network whose registry differs must have this table and its instances'
/// invoices agree with IT, not with this comment — parking on the wrong index
/// credits the wrong unit while still settling, which is silent and hard to
/// unpick later. Every dimension is independent and optional: a log
/// count or price-sheet rate that is absent counts as 0, so one code path settles
/// an EdgeNode invoice, a WindTunnel invoice, or any partial mix without a missing
/// key breaking it.

let BASE = "0"; // base fuel unit (HoloFuel) that funds host payment

/// Shape-check an agent pubkey. Delta entries are validated HERE rather than in
/// `runtime_input_signature.json`: a schema violation fails Rule 2 before this
/// script runs, so one malformed park would deadlock every settlement — a
/// consumable park is only deleted by a SUCCESSFUL execution. That is a typo's
/// blast radius on a qualified instance, and an attacker's on one that leaves
/// `list_publisher` qualified as `Any`. Skipping a
/// malformed entry here keeps a typo (or an attacker) from ever wedging the
/// agreement; a typo'd key simply never joins the list, and the unpayable-invoice
/// guard below then reports it loudly instead of silently discarding work.
fn is_agent_key(s) {
    type_of(s) == "string" && s.len() == 53 && s.starts_with("uhCAk")
}

// Per dimension: the metering unit index it credits, the price-sheet rate key,
// and the invoice log-count key.
let dims = [
    #{ unit: "2", rate: "base_per_gsp", count: "g"   },
    #{ unit: "3", rate: "base_per_st",  count: "s"   },
    #{ unit: "4", rate: "base_per_wt1", count: "wt1" },
    #{ unit: "5", rate: "base_per_wt2", count: "wt2" },
];

let price_sheet = get_data_blob(inputs.price_sheet_data_blob_hash.data);
let customer_alloc = consumed_inputs.edge_node_customer_spender_allocations;
let funds_owner = inputs.funds_owner_pubkey.data;

// The standing allow-list: carried from the previous execution, or seeded from
// initial_allow_list on the very first run.
let allowed = [];
if type_of(inputs.previous_execution.data) == "map" {
    let prev_carryover = inputs.previous_execution.data.output.carryover ?? #{};
    allowed = prev_carryover.allow_list ?? [];
} else {
    allowed = inputs.initial_allow_list.data;
}

// Apply this run's deltas: one gathering pass gates each park ONCE — the author
// check (a get_spend_links_author must_get per park) and the defensive payload
// reads live in a single place, so add and remove acceptance can never diverge —
// then all adds apply before all removes, deterministic regardless of park
// discovery order. A stranger's park is ignored, and a malformed payload from
// anyone can never break settlement: a consumable park is only deleted by a
// SUCCESSFUL execution, so a payload that could throw would deadlock the
// agreement.
let delta_adds = [];
let delta_removes = [];
for entry in consumed_inputs.allow_list_deltas {
    if get_spend_links_author(entry.link_hash) != funds_owner {
        continue;
    }
    if type_of(entry.data) != "map" {
        continue;
    }
    let adds = entry.data.add ?? [];
    if type_of(adds) == "array" {
        for a in adds {
            if is_agent_key(a) {
                delta_adds.push(a);
            }
        }
    }
    let removes = entry.data.remove ?? [];
    if type_of(removes) == "array" {
        for r in removes {
            if is_agent_key(r) {
                delta_removes.push(r);
            }
        }
    }
}
for a in delta_adds {
    if !allowed.contains(a) {
        allowed.push(a);
    }
}
if delta_removes.len() > 0 {
    allowed = allowed.filter(|x| !delta_removes.contains(x));
}

// Carried lock from the previous execution (auto-applied), and that execution's
// hash — the source a lock-funded host payment names. Prepended to the customer
// funding so the invoice loop draws it down before fresh parked credit.
let prev_source = ();
if type_of(inputs.previous_execution.data) == "map" {
    prev_source = inputs.previous_execution.data.id;
    // A prior run that fully spent its funding omits `locked`, so default it to
    // an empty map before indexing — `()[BASE]` would be a Rhai runtime error.
    // The carried amount stays the engine-written STRING end to end (floats are
    // for branching only — an f64 round trip can distort a fuel amount).
    let carried_locked = inputs.previous_execution.data.output.locked ?? #{};
    let carried = carried_locked[BASE] ?? "0";
    if to_num(carried) > 0.0 {
        let carried_amount = #{};
        carried_amount[BASE] = carried;
        customer_alloc.insert(0, #{ "data": #{ "amount": carried_amount, "source": prev_source } });
    }
}

// Total funding available this run (carried lock + fresh parks) and its sources,
// captured before any draw-down — shared by the unlock reclaim and the shortfall
// report. Exact fuel arithmetic (add_fuel) — an f64 accumulation can land one
// micro-unit off the conserved inputs and fail Rule 7.
let available_funding = "0";
let funding_sources = [];
for alloc in customer_alloc {
    available_funding = add_fuel(available_funding, alloc.data.amount[BASE] ?? "0");
    funding_sources.push(alloc.data.source);
}

// Note: consumed allow-list delta parks are NOT named as sources — validation
// accepts only parked SPENDS (or the prior RAVE) as allocation sources, and a
// fund-less ParkedData park needs no conservation naming.

// Unlock: return the whole held balance to the funds owner and emit no new lock.
// Runs before invoicing so a reclaim never settles host work; sources name every
// funding source so nothing is left unaccounted.
if type_of(inputs.unlock) == "map" && inputs.unlock.data == true {
    let out = [];
    if to_num(available_funding) > 0.0 {
        let amt = #{};
        amt[BASE] = available_funding;
        out.push(#{ "receiver": funds_owner, "amounts": amt, "sources": funding_sources });
    }
    return #{ "output": #{
        "unyt_allocation": out,
        "carryover": #{ "allow_list": allowed }
    } };
}

// Unpayable invoices: parked work for hosts the allow-list does not name —
// because the list was never seeded, because the host was removed mid-period
// after doing the work, or because a seeding key was mistyped. Settling would
// consume those parks, pay nothing, and Rule 5 would bar ever re-consuming
// them: the work would be destroyed unpaid and silently. Refuse instead, so
// the run is retryable after the list is corrected — or, when the customer
// really does mean to drop that work, let the executor say so explicitly with
// `discard_unpayable`. Deliberate, never silent.
let unpayable = 0;
for (value, vi) in consumed_inputs.invoice_payloads {
    for (payload, pi) in value.data {
        if !allowed.contains(payload.host_pub_key) {
            unpayable += 1;
        }
    }
}
if unpayable > 0 {
    let acknowledged = type_of(inputs.discard_unpayable) == "map"
        && inputs.discard_unpayable.data == true;
    if !acknowledged {
        throw "" + unpayable + " parked invoice(s) name hosts that are not on the allow-list"
            + " (the list currently names " + allowed.len() + "): settling would consume them"
            + " unpaid and they could never be re-submitted. Add the hosts with a list_publisher"
            + " delta park, or re-run with discard_unpayable=true to drop that work deliberately.";
    }
}

let final_unyt_allocation = [];
// Outstanding total across payable (allowed) invoices, in exact fuel strings
// like the draws themselves — an f64 sum can print a noisy or micro-short figure
// in the shortfall report.
let total_payment_expected = "0";
// Service-unit totals per dimension, accumulated across all invoices and
// credited to the funds owner on each dimension's own unit index.
let dimension_totals = #{ "2": 0.0, "3": 0.0, "4": 0.0, "5": 0.0 };
let able_to_pay = true;

// Resolve each dimension's rate once up front — the price sheet is Fixed for the
// whole execution, so this keeps the per-invoice loop from re-reading it when many
// invoices aggregate into a single settlement.
let rates = #{};
for dim in dims {
    rates[dim.unit] = to_num(price_sheet[dim.rate] ?? 0);
}

for (value, vi) in consumed_inputs.invoice_payloads {
    for (payload, pi) in value.data {
        // Sum this host's logged counts per dimension (absent count => 0).
        let host_counts = #{ "2": 0.0, "3": 0.0, "4": 0.0, "5": 0.0 };
        for (log, li) in payload.logs {
            for dim in dims {
                // absent count => "0" (indexing a missing object-map key yields ())
                host_counts[dim.unit] = host_counts[dim.unit] + to_num(log[dim.count] ?? "0");
            }
        }

        // Price the host: expected = Σ count_d × rate_d (rates resolved once above).
        let exp_amt = 0.0;
        for dim in dims {
            exp_amt = exp_amt + host_counts[dim.unit] * rates[dim.unit];
            dimension_totals[dim.unit] = dimension_totals[dim.unit] + host_counts[dim.unit];
        }

        // A host off the allow-list is never paid and never counts toward the
        // outstanding total (it must not inflate the shortfall report). Its
        // metered work STAYS in the dimension totals: the harvester parked those
        // service units without knowing the customer's list, and conservation
        // requires every consumed parked unit to land in an allocation.
        if !allowed.contains(payload.host_pub_key) {
            continue;
        }

        total_payment_expected = add_fuel(total_payment_expected, exp_amt.to_string());

        if able_to_pay && exp_amt > 0.0 {
            // Draw the invoice from as many customer allocations as needed, in
            // parked order (exact fuel arithmetic in the host): split funding —
            // e.g. 5 + 5 parked covering a 7 invoice — settles, where a
            // single-source match refused the run despite a sufficient total.
            // When even the total can't cover, nothing is drawn.
            let consume = customer_alloc.consume_allocations(BASE, exp_amt.to_string());
            if consume.covered {
                // Build with an indexed assignment: `#{ BASE: x }` would use the
                // literal key "BASE", not the value of BASE.
                let invoice_amount = #{};
                invoice_amount[BASE] = exp_amt.to_string();
                final_unyt_allocation.push(#{
                    "receiver": payload.host_pub_key,
                    "amounts": invoice_amount,
                    "sources": consume.sources
                });
            } else {
                // Can't cover this invoice — keep tallying the total so the error
                // reports the full outstanding amount, then stop allocating.
                able_to_pay = false;
            }
        }
        // exp_amt == 0 (all counts zero, or priced 0): emit no payment — a zero
        // MonetaryUnit allocation is uncollectable at the ledger, and nothing
        // was drawn so there is no source to name.
    }
}

if able_to_pay {
    // Unspent base-unit funding (carried lock + fresh parked remainder) to lock
    // for the next execution, and the sources that still carry a remainder.
    // Every source that still carries funds must stay named: a parked spend
    // counts as conserved input only when a `unyt_allocation` names its source
    // (fully-spent sources are already named on their host payments; the carried
    // lock rides forward as the predecessor's running balance and needs no
    // naming). They are named on the metering credit below.
    // Exact fuel arithmetic (add_fuel), floats only for the >0 branch: the
    // remainder becomes the committed lock, and an f64 sum that rounds even a
    // micro-unit below the exact inputs fails Rule 7 conservation.
    let remaining_customer_alloc = "0";
    let remaining_sources = [];
    for (alloc, i) in customer_alloc {
        let amt = alloc.data.amount[BASE] ?? "0";
        if to_num(amt) > 0.0 {
            remaining_customer_alloc = add_fuel(remaining_customer_alloc, amt);
            remaining_sources.push(alloc.data.source);
        }
    }

    // Credit each metered dimension's total to the FUNDS OWNER (the customer) on
    // its own unit index — the metering record of the service they paid for.
    // Pinning the receiver to funds_owner rather than the executor keeps the
    // record with the customer under the canonical harvester-executor instance.
    let metering_amounts = #{};
    for dim in dims {
        if dimension_totals[dim.unit] > 0.0 {
            metering_amounts[dim.unit] = dimension_totals[dim.unit].to_string();
        }
    }
    // Name every consumed invoice park and lock-funding remainder source on the
    // metering credit — also when nothing was metered (empty invoices, zero
    // counts, or no allowed host): the credit is then a NAME-ONLY allocation
    // with EMPTY amounts, so its sources still count as conserved input and the
    // run settles instead of failing Rule 7 with unnamed sources. Empty amounts,
    // never `{ BASE: "0" }` — a zero MonetaryUnit amount is uncollectable at the
    // ledger, while an empty-amounts allocation is recognized engine-side as
    // carrying no deposit at all.
    // (Non-empty amounts imply non-empty sources — dimension totals only
    // accumulate from invoice payloads, and every payload's link_hash is here —
    // so the emptiness check on sources alone suffices.)
    let metering_sources = consumed_inputs.invoice_payloads.map(|p| p.link_hash);
    for s in remaining_sources {
        metering_sources.push(s);
    }
    if metering_sources.len() > 0 {
        final_unyt_allocation.push(#{
            "receiver": funds_owner,
            "amounts": metering_amounts,
            "sources": metering_sources
        });
    }

    let output = #{
        "unyt_allocation": final_unyt_allocation,
        "carryover": #{ "allow_list": allowed }
    };
    if to_num(remaining_customer_alloc) > 0.0 {
        let locked = #{};
        locked[BASE] = remaining_customer_alloc;
        output.locked = locked;
    }
    return #{ "output": output };
} else {
    // The leading phrase is load-bearing: the parent app's sweettest matches on
    // it. The figures give the funder an actionable top-up:
    // shortfall = outstanding − available, all in exact fuel strings.
    let shortfall = sub_fuel(total_payment_expected, available_funding);
    throw "For execution to succeed, a payment of " + shortfall
        + " ZF must be sent to this agreement to settle outstanding invoices"
        + " (outstanding invoices total " + total_payment_expected
        + " ZF; available funding including any carried lock is " + available_funding + " ZF).";
}
